---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { parkingSources as sources, parkingReviewedAt } from '../data/parkingData';
import { buildLakeJourney, shuttleFaqs } from '../data/parkingPlanning';
const fallback = buildLakeJourney();
---
<BaseLayout title="Lake Louise & Moraine Lake Shuttles: Reservations & Route Choices" description="Compare Parks Park and Ride, Roam 8X, Lake Connector and authorised tours. Check the actual season, accessible transport, departure base and last return." lastUpdated={parkingReviewedAt}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: shuttleFaqs.map(faq => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: faq.question, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer } })) })} />
  <div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Lake Shuttle Planning' }]} /></div>
  <section class="page-hero"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1503614472-8c93d56e92ce?w=1600&q=80" alt="" class="page-hero-bg" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" /><div class="page-hero-content"><span class="badge">Choose the service before the ticket</span><h1>Lake Shuttle Reservations</h1><p>Plan Lake Louise and Moraine Lake around the actual season, departure point and return. Parks shuttles, Roam and commercial transfers are different journeys.</p><p class="image-note">Illustrative lake image; not a verified shuttle or current condition.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container shuttle-page">
    <aside class="source-notice"><h2>Season and source check</h2><p><strong>Checked <time datetime={parkingReviewedAt}>{parkingReviewedAt}</time>:</strong> Parks Canada’s published 2026 lake-shuttle season ended on 12 October. The pages reviewed do not verify a 2027 Parks reservation-launch or service-start date. A passed reservation date does not mean buses are running.</p><p>Use the <a href={sources.lakes.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">official Parks lake-access page ↗</a> and the <a href={sources.roam8x.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">current Roam 8X schedule/reservations ↗</a> for your actual date. This page contains planning guidance, not live seats or a countdown.</p></aside>

    <h2>Which journey are you building?</h2>
    <form id="lake-journey-form" class="journey-controls" aria-label="Lake transport choices" hidden><div class="choice-grid"><label>Your starting base<select id="lake-base"><option value="banff">Banff</option><option value="canmore">Canmore</option><option value="lake-louise">Lake Louise</option><option value="other">Another base / driving in</option></select></label><label>Intended destination<select id="lake-destination"><option value="both">Both lakes</option><option value="louise">Lake Louise only</option><option value="moraine">Moraine Lake</option></select></label><label>Seasonal context<select id="lake-season"><option value="unsure">Date / season not settled</option><option value="winter">Snow season</option><option value="summer">Summer visitor season</option></select></label></div><fieldset><legend>Extra arrangements</legend><label><input type="checkbox" id="lake-mobility" /> Accessible vehicle, mobility device or assistance</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="lake-early" /> Early activity / Alpine Start enquiry</label></fieldset><button class="btn btn-outline" type="reset">Reset choices</button><p>These choices add planning questions; they do not confirm an operating service, ticket or suitable route.</p></form>
    <p id="lake-journey-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">The complete service comparison and booking steps are shown below.</p><section class="journey-plan" aria-labelledby="lake-plan-heading"><h3 id="lake-plan-heading">{fallback.heading}</h3><ol id="lake-plan-steps">{fallback.steps.map(step => <li>{step}</li>)}</ol></section><noscript><p>All service descriptions, booking steps, access questions and source links remain available below without JavaScript.</p></noscript>

    <h2>Five services to keep distinct</h2><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Lake transport service comparison" tabindex="0"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">Where the journey starts</th><th scope="col">What to establish before booking</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Regular Parks reserved shuttle</th><td>Lake Louise Ski Resort Park and Ride, after check-in. This is not the village or lakeshore.</td><td>Actual seasonal dates, selected first lake, departure window, party and return. The reviewed ticket includes the Lake Connector and return to Park and Ride; park admission is separate. <a href={sources.lakes.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks service ↗</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Roam 8X</th><td>Banff to Lake Louise village and lakeshore, on the actual timetable.</td><td>Correct stop and outbound/return product. A normal 8X fare is not a Moraine Lake ticket. Check connections from Canmore separately. <a href={sources.roam8x.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">8X route ↗</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Parks Lake Connector</th><td>Between Lake Louise lakeshore and Moraine Lake during its operating season.</td><td>Eligible ticket and both return legs. Parks requires the checked-in shuttle ticket or a valid Roam Super Pass; do not arrive expecting a standalone walk-up connector ticket. <a href={sources.lakeFaq.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Connector FAQ ↗</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Roam Super Pass</th><td>A date-valid Roam journey through Banff and 8X to the Louise lakeshore, followed by the eligible connector.</td><td>The product’s actual season, 8X reservation and connector entitlement. Its reviewed page states June–October 2026, already ended; this does not establish a 2027 product or winter service. <a href={sources.superpass.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Super Pass terms ↗</a></td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">Alpine Start</th><td>The published 2026 product departed the upper Lake Louise lakeshore lot, with separate paid parking and check-in.</td><td>Verify whether it is offered for the intended year and its own return instructions. It was not the regular Park and Ride departure and had no accessible vehicle in 2026. <a href={sources.lakeFaq.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Alpine Start details ↗</a></td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div>

    <section class="guide-section"><h2>Moraine access is restricted year-round</h2><p>Moraine Lake Road is closed to personal vehicles year-round. Parks lists its shuttles, licensed commercial operators with a Moraine Lake Road Licence of Occupation and registered Moraine Lake Lodge guests as authorised access. Use the exact operator or property instructions. A normal rental, an early arrival or an accessible placard is not a general road-access exception.</p><p>Commercial access permission is not a promise that every trip runs, reaches the lake in all weather, or collects at your hotel. Confirm the actual pickup and route. Check the <a href="https://carfreebanff.ca/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">licensed transport information linked by Parks ↗</a> and the <a href={sources.lakes.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">official access rules ↗</a>.</p><h3>Winter is a separate plan</h3><p>The ended summer bus system does not supply a winter Moraine visit. The official winter description for Moraine Lake Road has route limits and avalanche context before the lake. This guide does not offer a winter cycling or walking workaround. Compare an independently planned <a href="/winter">winter outing</a> or a Lake Louise-only visit with its own current route, rink and transport checks.</p><p><a href="https://parks.canada.ca/pn-np/ab/banff/activ/raquette-snowshoeing/lakelouise" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks winter-route descriptions ↗</a></p></section>

    <section class="guide-section"><h2>Make a reservation you can actually use</h2><ol class="booking-steps"><li><strong>Identify the date, destination and party.</strong> Include every traveller and the intended first lake. Decide whether the trip is a short visit or includes a walk, hike or other timed booking.</li><li><strong>Confirm the correct year’s programme.</strong> Check the official release dates, service period and change/cancellation terms. The reviewed Parks 2026 process used an initial release and a two-day rolling release at Mountain Time; do not apply its dates or percentages to an unannounced year.</li><li><strong>Use the correct booking provider.</strong> Parks and Roam reservations are separate systems. Sign in and check account access beforehand using a supported option; GCKey is not the only Parks sign-in method.</li><li><strong>Choose the exact departure.</strong> Regular Parks reservations require Park and Ride check-in and the selected first lake. Roam boards at its actual stop. Alpine Start, if offered, has different departure instructions.</li><li><strong>Resolve equipment and access before paying.</strong> Tell the operator about mobility devices, assistance, children, strollers, unusual baggage or equipment. Ask how the whole party travels together and what can actually be carried.</li><li><strong>Book and retain the return.</strong> Record the last usable connector, bus, onward connection and car-park access time. A trail or attraction must finish with enough time to reach the boarding point.</li></ol><p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={sources.reservations.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open official Parks Reservation Service ↗</a> <a class="btn btn-outline" href={sources.roam8x.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Check Roam 8X reservations ↗</a></p><p>These links open the provider’s service; no reservation is submitted by this page.</p></section>

    <section class="guide-section"><h2>Accessible vehicles, children and final approaches</h2><div class="planning-grid"><article><h3>Regular accessible shuttle</h3><p>The reviewed regular Parks service dispatches an accessible vehicle on request at Park and Ride check-in with a purchased ticket. Companion seats and device arrangements need confirmation. Its published 2026 Alpine Start service had no accessible vehicle; ask about the actual future season instead of assuming the two products match.</p><p><a href={sources.lakeFaq.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Parks accessibility FAQ ↗</a></p></article><article><h3>The final path matters</h3><p>An accessible bus or parking placard does not assess snow, kerbs, dock/rink approaches or the whole lakeshore route. Moraine has no accessible parking in the reviewed Parks information. Confirm washrooms, waiting/rest places and assistance for the actual date.</p><p><a href="/accessible-trails">Compare access features and questions →</a></p></article><article><h3>Family and equipment check</h3><p>Ask the selected provider about child tickets, restraint rules, stroller storage, equipment and boarding assistance. Allow for toilets, waiting, food and warm layers. A tour’s advertised duration may omit your journey to its meeting point.</p><p><a href="/packing-list">Build a packing checklist →</a></p></article></div></section>

    <section class="guide-section"><h2>Plan the last return before the first departure</h2><ul><li>Save the exact stop and the destination of each return bus. A Park and Ride return, a Louise lakeshore return and a Banff return are different.</li><li>For Canmore, check the final onward Route 3 connection; arrival in Banff does not complete that trip.</li><li>Allow for queues and the walk from the activity to the stop. Do not make the last departure your target finishing time.</li><li>Download tickets and instructions. Moraine has no dependable mobile connection for arranging an improvised ride, and a paid parking area can have gate or retrieval restrictions.</li><li>If your activity cannot fit the published transport window, arrange an authorised alternative before booking. Do not rely on a lodge for shelter, a lift or an unconfirmed late pickup.</li></ul><p><a href="/car-free-banff">Compare the full transport chain</a> · <a href="/parking">Destination parking planner</a> · <a href={sources.roam3.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Canmore–Banff stop and service checks ↗</a></p></section>

    <section class="guide-section"><h2>If your first choice is unavailable</h2><p>Use the actual year’s official release and cancellation process, compare another authorised transport product, or choose a Lake Louise-only or town-based plan. A hike from Moraine, including Consolation Lakes, still depends on reaching its trailhead; it is not an access-free substitute.</p><p>A different lake or trail also needs its own road, parking, route, weather and return checks. Use <a href="/things-to-do">sightseeing choices</a> or <a href="/alternatives">outing comparisons</a> to make a separate plan rather than assuming an uncrowded alternative.</p><div class="affiliate-note"><h3>Optional marketplace search</h3><p>We may earn a commission from a booking through this affiliate link. It is a GetYourGuide search, not a verified operator, current seat, road permission or confirmed pickup.</p><a href="https://www.getyourguide.com/banff-l284/?q=moraine+lake&partner_id=QW960HO" target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored">Search Moraine Lake tours on GetYourGuide ↗</a><p>Read the actual product’s dates, route, licence/access arrangements, party eligibility, pickup, return and cancellation terms.</p></div></section>
    <section class="guide-section"><h2>Lake-shuttle questions</h2>{shuttleFaqs.map(faq => <details><summary>{faq.question}</summary><p>{faq.answer}</p></details>)}</section>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  import { buildLakeJourney } from '../data/parkingPlanning';
  const form = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#lake-journey-form');
  const base = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#lake-base');
  const destination = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#lake-destination');
  const season = document.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('#lake-season');
  const mobility = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#lake-mobility');
  const early = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('#lake-early');
  const heading = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#lake-plan-heading');
  const steps = document.querySelector<HTMLOListElement>('#lake-plan-steps');
  const status = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#lake-journey-status');
  if (form && base && destination && season && mobility && early && heading && steps && status) {
    function updateJourney() {
      const plan = buildLakeJourney({ base: base.value, destination: destination.value, season: season.value, mobility: mobility.checked, early: early.checked });
      heading.textContent = plan.heading;
      steps.replaceChildren(...plan.steps.map(text => { const item = document.createElement('li'); item.textContent = text; return item; }));
      status.textContent = 'Journey checks updated. The complete service comparison remains below; current operation and reservations must be checked with the provider.';
    }
    form.addEventListener('submit', event => event.preventDefault());
    form.addEventListener('change', updateJourney);
    form.addEventListener('reset', event => { event.preventDefault(); base.value = 'banff'; destination.value = 'both'; season.value = 'unsure'; mobility.checked = early.checked = false; updateJourney(); });
    form.hidden = false;
    updateJourney();
  }
</script>
<style>
  [hidden]{display:none!important}.shuttle-page{max-width:1100px}.shuttle-page p,.shuttle-page li{line-height:1.75}.image-note{font-size:.76rem!important;line-height:1.5!important;opacity:.9}.source-notice,.journey-plan,.affiliate-note{padding:1.5rem;border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--color-bg-alt);border-left:4px solid var(--color-accent);margin:1.5rem 0}.source-notice h2{margin-top:0}.journey-controls{padding:1.3rem;border:1px solid #bacbc0;border-radius:var(--radius);margin:1.3rem 0}.choice-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem}.choice-grid label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.4rem;font-weight:700}select{font:inherit;padding:.65rem;border:1px solid #94a99c;border-radius:6px;background:white;color:var(--color-text);width:100%}fieldset{margin:1rem 0;border:1px solid #c3cec7;padding:1rem}legend{font-weight:700}fieldset label{display:block;margin:.65rem 0;line-height:1.6}input[type=checkbox]{margin-right:.5rem}.journey-plan li,.booking-steps li{margin:.9rem 0}.guide-section{margin-top:2.8rem}.planning-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,280px),1fr));gap:1.3rem}.planning-grid article{padding:1.2rem;border:1px solid #c7d3cb;border-radius:var(--radius)}.table-scroll{overflow-x:auto;border:1px solid #c7d3cb;border-radius:8px}table{border-collapse:collapse;min-width:700px;width:100%;font-size:.9rem}th,td{text-align:left;vertical-align:top;padding:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid #c7d3cb;line-height:1.7}thead th{background:var(--color-bg-alt)}details{padding:1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d1dbd4}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible,.table-scroll:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-primary);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:600px){.source-notice,.journey-plan,.affiliate-note,.journey-controls{padding:1rem}.btn{white-space:normal}}
</style>
